    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d501">

                <pb facs="0613" n="603" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg603"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/1399: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-08T10:00:00+07:00">August 8, 1942—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 8—7:33 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>920. Embassy’s 836, July 13, noon. Embassy understands from Kwok, Director of
                    Foreign Trade Office of NRC,<anchor n="18" xml:id="d501-f1"/> that agreement has
                    been reached with Russians by Wong Wen-hao (who has not yet returned from
                    northwest) to exchange during this year 2,000 tons strategic materials desired
                    by Russian for equal weight of supplies for China (primarily gasoline) the point
                    of exchange to be Hami, transportation to be by truck.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d501-f1" n="18" xml:id="d501-f1-content">
                <p>National Resources Commission, Chinese Ministry of Economic Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
